_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 381631, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FLLydTz4Xu8nxzxK8Chxyn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 387405, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CyQrzyHij9QNtYND66QheC", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nUpgrades `fastjson` from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix **CVE-2026-31337** (high severity): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays.\n\n- Affected: `<2.9.4`, `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`\n- Fixed in: `2.9.4`, `3.1.0`\n\nI chose 2.9.4 because it is the smallest upgrade that fixes the issue and stays on the 2.x major line, so it avoids the risk of breaking changes from 3.x.\n\n## Changes\n- `requirements.txt`: `fastjson==2.8.0` -> `fastjson==2.9.4`\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: added a security entry under Unreleased\n\n## Testing\nCI run `ci-0001` passed on commit a7ffe29fb7.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 418305, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CyQrzyHij9QNtYND66QheC", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 418305, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CyQrzyHij9QNtYND66QheC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 421193, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0179yvfKgdBQ9x69HGTY9MDB", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 421493, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0179yvfKgdBQ9x69HGTY9MDB", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 421493, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0179yvfKgdBQ9x69HGTY9MDB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 429873, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The vulnerability:** The advisory rates it high severity: deeply nested arrays can make the parser recurse without limit. Versions below 2.9.4 and 3.0.x are affected, and 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 fix it. I picked 2.9.4 because it's the smallest fix and stays on version 2, so it avoids the risk of breaking changes from moving to 3.x.\n- **The change:** On a new branch, `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, I updated the fastjson pin in `requirements.txt` and added a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md` (commit a7ffe29fb7).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **The PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. When I opened it, alex wasn't added as a reviewer, so I requested his review separately, and that went through.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking up the advisory and checking the repository layout.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016Co9DrXahsQie8vdpt8M4C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011E6jnRwuQKvNyhmDwVb4a1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_files", "ty