e": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FLLydTz4Xu8nxzxK8Chxyn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on a7ffe29fb7. Opening the PR:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CyQrzyHij9QNtYND66QheC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nUpgrades `fastjson` from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix **CVE-2026-31337** (high severity): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays.\n\n- Affected: `<2.9.4`, `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`\n- Fixed in: `2.9.4`, `3.1.0`\n\nI chose 2.9.4 because it is the smallest upgrade that fixes the issue and stays on the 2.x major line, so it avoids the risk of breaking changes from 3.x.\n\n## Changes\n- `requirements.txt`: `fastjson==2.8.0` -> `fastjson==2.9.4`\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: added a security entry under Unreleased\n\n## Testing\nCI run `ci-0001` passed on commit a7ffe29fb7.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but its reviewers list came back empty, so I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0179yvfKgdBQ9x69HGTY9MDB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The vulnerability:** The advisory rates it high severity: deeply nested arrays can make the parser recurse without limit. Versions below 2.9.4 and 3.0.x are affected, and 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 fix it. I picked 2.9.4 because it's the smallest fix and stays on version 2, so it avoids the risk of breaking changes from moving to 3.x.\n- **The change:** On a new branch, `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, I updated the fastjson pin in `requirements.txt` and added a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md` (commit a7ffe29fb7).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **The PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. When I opened it, alex wasn't added as a reviewer, so I requested his review separately, and that went through.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}